WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.933 --> 00:00:18.376
followed Ivan and Kelsey off the school bus and looked around nervously.

2
00:00:21.038 --> 00:00:24.040
The field was crowded with people in historical costumes.

3
00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:29.464
There were women in long dresses and bonnets, and men in straw hats and leather boots.

4
00:00:30.552 --> 00:00:32.353
"Welcome to Pioneer Days!"

5
00:00:32.694 --> 00:00:34.335
Mrs. Manning, the teacher, said.

6
00:00:34.355 --> 00:00:41.079
"In the 1800s around 400,000 people left their homes in the East.

7
00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:45.983
They wanted to settle on open land and find new opportunities.

8
00:00:47.604 --> 00:00:52.827
So these pioneers traveled across America in covered wagons to settle in the West."

9
00:00:52.847 --> 00:00:56.290
"What kind of person wants to dress up like a pioneer?"

10
00:00:56.570 --> 00:00:57.330
Kelsey said.

11
00:00:57.350 --> 00:01:00.701
"Yeah," Damon mumbled.

12
00:01:02.602 --> 00:01:07.026
He spotted his mother standing by an open fire, wearing her homemade outfit.

13
00:01:08.267 --> 00:01:12.330
Before his friends could notice her, Damon pointed wildly across the field.

14
00:01:13.211 --> 00:01:14.212
"Look at the oxen!"

15
00:01:14.232 --> 00:01:19.216
"Wow!" Ivan stared at the huge animals.

16
00:01:19.236 --> 00:01:21.998
"Why are cows pulling a wagon?

17
00:01:23.019 --> 00:01:24.480
Why not just use horses?"

18
00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:27.683
"They're oxen, not cows, Ivan!"

19
00:01:27.963 --> 00:01:29.044
Mrs. Manning said.

20
00:01:29.796 --> 00:01:37.061
"Pioneers used oxen instead of horses to pull wagons because they're strong, tough—" "And slow!"

21
00:01:38.402 --> 00:01:40.864
Kelsey giggled as the oxen trudged past.

22
00:01:40.884 --> 00:01:44.326
"See the cream pail on the side of the wagon?"

23
00:01:44.606 --> 00:01:45.727
Mrs. Manning said.

24
00:01:45.747 --> 00:01:49.829
"The wagon's motion churns the cream into butter."

25
00:01:50.890 --> 00:01:54.553
Damon noticed Mom waving at him, but he pretended not to see.

26
00:01:54.573 --> 00:01:57.875
"Let's go learn about the Native Americans!"

27
00:01:58.215 --> 00:01:59.276
he said hurriedly.

28
00:02:00.564 --> 00:02:02.145
Mrs. Manning checked the time.

29
00:02:02.165 --> 00:02:04.166
"It's lunchtime now.

30
00:02:04.446 --> 00:02:06.967
We're having an authentic pioneer lunch!"

31
00:02:17.951 --> 00:02:20.372
"Shouldn't we see the cow-milking station first?"

32
00:02:20.712 --> 00:02:22.013
Damon asked hopefully.

33
00:02:22.033 --> 00:02:24.334
"After lunch," Mrs.

34
00:02:24.394 --> 00:02:25.674
Manning said firmly.

35
00:02:25.694 --> 00:02:29.556
"Damon!" Kelsey said suddenly.

36
00:02:30.132 --> 00:02:31.113
"Isn't that your mom?"

37
00:02:32.514 --> 00:02:34.295
Damon wished he could disappear.

38
00:02:34.315 --> 00:02:38.297
"Hello, everyone!"

39
00:02:39.057 --> 00:02:41.919
Mom smiled cheerfully as she handed out plates of food.

40
00:02:41.939 --> 00:02:45.741
"Everything you're eating here was cooked over an open fire.

41
00:02:47.642 --> 00:02:50.684
Most pioneers didn't pack their heavy stoves in the wagons.

42
00:02:51.565 --> 00:02:54.146
So they cooked in iron pots called Dutch ovens."

43
00:02:55.147 --> 00:02:57.048
She gestured at the pots by the fire.

44
00:02:58.244 --> 00:03:01.945
"They baked bread and biscuits in these, and cooked beans and stews.

45
00:03:02.725 --> 00:03:08.707
They had to pack enough flour, beans, rice, cornmeal, and bacon for six months of hard traveling.

46
00:03:09.667 --> 00:03:14.248
Sometimes they had to clean the bacon before they ate it, to remove mold or bugs."

47
00:03:14.268 --> 00:03:16.829
"Moldy bacon?"

48
00:03:17.049 --> 00:03:17.869
Kelsey said.

49
00:03:17.889 --> 00:03:19.950
"Bugs? Yuck!"

50
00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:22.190
Ivan pretended to throw up.

51
00:03:23.051 --> 00:03:25.471
"Moldy bacon was the least of their worries!"

52
00:03:25.791 --> 00:03:27.672
Damon suddenly heard himself say.

53
00:03:28.768 --> 00:03:31.851
"The pioneers had to survive storms and diseases.

54
00:03:33.292 --> 00:03:37.135
They turned their wagons into boats to float across flooded rivers.

55
00:03:38.076 --> 00:03:41.699
Sometimes they even lowered them down cliffs on ropes.

56
00:03:42.619 --> 00:03:46.542
When they finally settled, they could only use what they had brought with them!

57
00:03:47.383 --> 00:03:52.767
They had to build their own houses, grow their own food, and make their own clothes.

58
00:03:53.748 --> 00:03:54.989
Nothing was easy for them!"

59
00:03:56.150 --> 00:03:58.092
His friends blinked at him in surprise.

60
00:03:58.688 --> 00:03:59.608
Damon flushed.

61
00:04:00.669 --> 00:04:02.709
Now they were really going to tease him!

62
00:04:02.729 --> 00:04:06.050
"Wow!" Kelsey said finally.

63
00:04:06.070 --> 00:04:09.171
"I guess the pioneers were pretty tough."

64
00:04:09.191 --> 00:04:12.792
"And smart," Ivan said.

65
00:04:12.812 --> 00:04:15.753
"How do you know all this, Damon?"

66
00:04:16.633 --> 00:04:20.314
"My mom brings me to Pioneer Days every year," Damon admitted.

67
00:04:20.334 --> 00:04:23.235
"I guess I've learned a few things!"

68
00:04:23.255 --> 00:04:26.816
"These biscuits are delicious!"

69
00:04:27.136 --> 00:04:28.837
Kelsey said with her mouth full.

70
00:04:28.857 --> 00:04:33.380
"Can you show me how to make them?"

71
00:04:34.301 --> 00:04:38.183
Maybe seeing Mom in her pioneer outfit was not so bad after all.

72
00:04:38.203 --> 00:04:41.045
"Sure." Damon grinned.

73
00:04:41.065 --> 00:04:44.207
"But only if you dress up like a pioneer!"
